  "summary": "Applying the 2026-09-01 revision notice: (a) the revised certified rent roll supersedes the prior roll, with Suite 002 monthly rent +$225 to $14,825 and all other lease details preserved; (b) sizing rate +75 bps to 7.75%; (c) cap rate +25 bps to 6.5000%; payoff, expenses, reserves, and LTV/DSCR/DY limits unchanged. Occupancy is unchanged at 7/8 units (87.50%) and 154,060/176,060 SF (87.50%). Underwriting produces GPR $1,404,600, EGI $1,337,170, NOI (pre-reserve) $904,270.90, NCF $901,870.90, and a 6.5000% capitalization value of $13,911,860.00. Debt sizing at 7.75% floor, 30-yr monthly amortization, produces a maximum loan of $8,392,476 with DSCR the binding constraint (LTV cap $9,042,709; DY cap $10,020,788). After $7.8M payoff, $45K closing, and 1% origination (~$83,925), net cash-out is +$463,551 \u2014 reduced by ~$614K from v1 but still positive; no refinance shortfall. All eight risk flags retain their v1 polarities; the sizing-floor gap widens (90 bps \u2192 165 bps) and cash-out cushion narrows.",
